   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the not-for-profit corporation law, in relation to exempting\nthe Varna Volunteer Fire Company, Inc., from the forty-five percent limit on\nnon-resident members",
    "basePrintNo": "S8642",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8642-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1402, N-PC L",
    "lawSection": "Not-for-Profit Corporation Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8642\n\nSPONSOR: WEBB\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the not-for-profit corporation law, in relation to\nexempting the Varna Volunteer Fire Company, Inc., from the forty-five\npercent limit on non-resident members\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nExempts the Varna Volunteer Fire Company, Inc., within the Town of\nDryden, Tompkins County from the forty-five percent limit on non-resi-\ndent members\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one waives the Varna Volunteer Fire Company from the provision\nof law limiting non-resident members in a fire corporation to forty-five\npercent of the actual membership.\n\nSection two provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Varna Volunteer Fire Company serves the hamlets of Varna and Ellis\nHollow within the Town of Dryden. Like most small fire departments, the\nVarna Volunteer Fire Company had difficulty recruiting new volunteers\nwithin their 16.7 square mile fire protection district.  Their solution\nwas to reach out to the two local colleges, Cornell University and Itha-\nca College, located just beyond the Town's border in Ithaca to recruit\nnew members. Their efforts have been successful in rebuilding the fire\ncompany ranks with young, active responders enabling the fire company to\nprovide critical first response services to the communities they serve.\nThis legislation is necessary to ensure compliance with state law that\nplaces a limit on non-resident membership for volunteer fire depart-\nments.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.   \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
